		<title>Full segment from 11/20 WWE SmackDown: Jim Duggan selected for Team USA, then backs out</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398074-full-segment-from-11-20-wwe-smackdown-jim-duggan-selected-for-team-usa-then-backs-out/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398074-full-segment-from-11-20-wwe-smackdown-jim-duggan-selected-for-team-usa-then-backs-out/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:25:05 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Jim Duggan]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Smackdown]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Survivor Series]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Team USA]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398074</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>WWE has posted the full segment from Friday&#8217;s (11/20) SmackDown, featuring WWE Hall of Famer &#8216;Hacksaw&#8217; Jim Duggan&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398074-full-segment-from-11-20-wwe-smackdown-jim-duggan-selected-for-team-usa-then-backs-out/">Full segment from 11/20 WWE SmackDown: Jim Duggan selected for Team USA, then backs out</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">WWE has posted the full segment from Friday&#8217;s (11/20) <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-smackdown-results/398035-wwe-smackdown-results-11-20-26-wargames-advantage-match/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">SmackDown</a>, featuring WWE Hall of Famer &#8216;Hacksaw&#8217; Jim Duggan being selected as the fifth member for Team USA at Survivor Series.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Co-Team USA Captain picked Duggan. However Team USA Captain Cody Rhodes was reluctant, but then agreed after Punk pleaded his case. After Punk showed Duggan a video package of Team Mexico, Duggan quickly backed out and left the ring abruptly.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Later in the show, Punk and Rhodes were out in the back parking lot area of the venue, in which Rhodes told Punk that he may have someone as the fifth member, but is making Punk wait until Monday&#8217;s Raw.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<iframe loading="lazy" title="FULL SEGMENT: CM Punk and Cody Rhodes try to find fifth Team USA member: SmackDown, Nov. 20, 2026" width="1200" height="675" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/05GwEI40X5M?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398074-full-segment-from-11-20-wwe-smackdown-jim-duggan-selected-for-team-usa-then-backs-out/">Full segment from 11/20 WWE SmackDown: Jim Duggan selected for Team USA, then backs out</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398074-full-segment-from-11-20-wwe-smackdown-jim-duggan-selected-for-team-usa-then-backs-out/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Tony Khan announces Red Velvet is not cleared to compete at ROH Final Battle, Women&#8217;s TV Title vacated</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/398066-tony-khan-announces-red-velvet-is-not-cleared-to-compete-at-roh-final-battle-womens-tv-title-vacated/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/398066-tony-khan-announces-red-velvet-is-not-cleared-to-compete-at-roh-final-battle-womens-tv-title-vacated/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 02:48:16 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Misc. News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[ROH News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Final Battle]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Red Velvet]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[ROH]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Women's TV Title Vacated]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398066</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Tony Khan announced on social media Friday, that Red Velvet is not medically cleared to compete at the&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/398066-tony-khan-announces-red-velvet-is-not-cleared-to-compete-at-roh-final-battle-womens-tv-title-vacated/">Tony Khan announces Red Velvet is not cleared to compete at ROH Final Battle, Women&#8217;s TV Title vacated</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Tony Khan announced on social media Friday, that Red Velvet is not medically cleared to compete at the ROH Final Battle pay-per-view next month and has vacated the Women&#8217;s World TV Championship.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Khan said that a tournament will determine the new champion, with the finals taking place at Final Battle.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Zayda Steel vs. Robyn Renegade, Isla Dawn vs. Viva Van, Trish Adora vs. Dani Luna, and Vert Vixen vs. Mina Shirakawa are part of the tournament quarterfinal matchups.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Below is the current lineup for Final Battle.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-ROH Women’s Championship Match: Athena defends against Hyan</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-ROH World Television Championship Three-Way Match: Action Andretti vs. Adam Priest vs. ELP</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-ROH World Championship Survival of the Fittest Match: Bandido defends against TBD</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-ROH Women’s World Television Championship Match: TBA vs. TBA</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list"></ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The ROH Final Battle PPV will take place at the <a href="https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=%2Fg%2F11rsfx42bm">Boeing Center at Tech Port</a> in San Antonio, Texas.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="zxx" dir="ltr"><a href="https://t.co/tMmRVX1IeI">https://t.co/tMmRVX1IeI</a></p>&mdash; Tony Khan (@TonyKhan) <a href="https://x.com/TonyKhan/status/2123945133867520395?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 21, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/398066-tony-khan-announces-red-velvet-is-not-cleared-to-compete-at-roh-final-battle-womens-tv-title-vacated/">Tony Khan announces Red Velvet is not cleared to compete at ROH Final Battle, Women&#8217;s TV Title vacated</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/398066-tony-khan-announces-red-velvet-is-not-cleared-to-compete-at-roh-final-battle-womens-tv-title-vacated/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Two releases from TNA Wrestling confirmed</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/398060-two-releases-from-tna-wrestling-confirmed/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/398060-two-releases-from-tna-wrestling-confirmed/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 02:32:44 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Impact News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact Wrestling News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[released]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[The Personal Concierge]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TNA]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398060</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>TNA has announced in a statement, that The Personal Concierge (George Iceman) and the promotion have come to&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/398060-two-releases-from-tna-wrestling-confirmed/">Two releases from TNA Wrestling confirmed</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA has announced in a statement, that The Personal Concierge (George Iceman) and the promotion have come to terms on a release effective immediately.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The company has also announced referee Michael Romo has left as well.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>“TNA Wrestling has come to terms on the release of The Personal Concierge, effective immediately. In addition, referee Michael Romo will no longer be working for TNA Wrestling. No further comment will be made. We wish both the best in their future endeavors.”</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Personal Concierge was the mouthpiece of The Elegance Brand faction, which had consisted of Ash by Elegance, Heather by Elegance, M by Elegance and Mr. Elegance. TNA did an angle back on the October 29 episode of IMPACT, where Mr. Elegance quit the group. Ash had stepped away from the ring, as she and her husband are expecting their first child together.  TNA did an other angle with Elegance Brand at Thursday&#8217;s <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-results/398007-tna-impact-on-amc-results-11-19-26-tna-world-title-and-more/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">IMPACT television tapings</a>. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Personal Concierge&#8217;s contract was reportedly set to expire by the end of this year.  </p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/398060-two-releases-from-tna-wrestling-confirmed/">Two releases from TNA Wrestling confirmed</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/398060-two-releases-from-tna-wrestling-confirmed/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>TNA Thanksgiving Special not airing on AMC in the United States</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/398040-tna-thanksgiving-special-not-airing-on-amc-in-the-united-states/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/398040-tna-thanksgiving-special-not-airing-on-amc-in-the-united-states/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:35:30 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Impact News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact Wrestling News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Thanksgiving Special]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TNA]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398040</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>TNA has announced that its Thanksgiving Special episode of IMPACT will not broadcast on AMC in the United&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/398040-tna-thanksgiving-special-not-airing-on-amc-in-the-united-states/">TNA Thanksgiving Special not airing on AMC in the United States</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA has announced that its Thanksgiving Special episode of IMPACT will not broadcast on AMC in the United States.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The cable network&#8217;s <a href="https://www.amc.com/schedule/?tz=ET&amp;from=2026-11-26&amp;bc=east">schedule</a> notes that the film <em>The Great Outdoors</em> will air during IMPACT&#8217;s usual time slot, as part of a movie marathon for the holiday.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The special holiday episode, featuring &#8220;never before seen matches,&#8221; will instead air on AMC+ in the United States, Sportsnet 360 in Canada, and TNA+ worldwide as normal.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">PROGRAMMING NOTE: Due to the Thanksgiving holiday, next week&#39;s Thanksgiving Special episode of <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/TNAiMPACT?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#TNAiMPACT</a> will not broadcast on <a href="https://x.com/AMC_TV?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">@AMC_TV</a>, but will be available on <a href="https://x.com/AMCPlus?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">@AMCPlus</a>. <br><br>The episode will broadcast on TNA+ worldwide and <a href="https://x.com/Sportsnet?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">@Sportsnet</a> 360 in Canada as normal. <a href="https://t.co/gx1Bx6hHN2">pic.twitter.com/gx1Bx6hHN2</a></p>&mdash; TNA Wrestling (@ThisIsTNA) <a href="https://x.com/ThisIsTNA/status/2123853890688840048?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 20, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/398040-tna-thanksgiving-special-not-airing-on-amc-in-the-united-states/">TNA Thanksgiving Special not airing on AMC in the United States</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/398040-tna-thanksgiving-special-not-airing-on-amc-in-the-united-states/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>WWE SmackDown Results &#8211; 11/20/26 (WarGames Advantage Match)</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-smackdown-results/398035-wwe-smackdown-results-11-20-26-wargames-advantage-match/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-smackdown-results/398035-wwe-smackdown-results-11-20-26-wargames-advantage-match/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Roy Nemer]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:14:57 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE Smackdown Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[11/20/26 WWE SmackDown Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Smackdown]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398035</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>WWE SmackDown ResultsNovember 20, 2026Evansville, Indiana (Ford Center)Commentary: Michael Cole and Corey GravesResults by: Roy Nemer of Wrestleview.com&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-smackdown-results/398035-wwe-smackdown-results-11-20-26-wargames-advantage-match/">WWE SmackDown Results &#8211; 11/20/26 (WarGames Advantage Match)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<figure class="wp-block-image is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="207" height="84" src="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/image-38.png" alt="" class="wp-image-354572" style="aspect-ratio:2.4642857142857144;width:207px;height:auto"/></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>WWE SmackDown Results<br>November 20, 2026<br>Evansville, Indiana (Ford Center)<br>Commentary: Michael Cole and Corey Graves<br>Results by: Roy Nemer of Wrestleview.com</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Owens says he needs a match against Sami Zayn for the WWE title and there is only one man that can make that happen, Owens says Nick Aldis but out comes Gunther.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Owens says he&#8217;s not Nick Aldis and Gunther says he understands, he says Owens should have stayed on the shelf because he does not belong in a world where Gunther wants to be WWE Champion. Gunther says unlike SummerSlam, he won&#8217;t let Owens get in the way again. Owens tells Gunther that Gunther is complaining that Owens was added to the match that Gunther was also added to at SummerSlam and if he is serious.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Gunther says he takes all of this very serious, he takes standing in the ring very serious, he takes being a World champion very serious, he takes ending careers very serious. Gunther says if Owens doesn&#8217;t want to end up on the operation table, he should take Gunther&#8217;s presence very seriously. He tells Owens that he is not a monster, he will give him a chance that he did not give Finn Balor and that is to get out of his ring and to stay out of his way.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Owens says fine and leaves the ring. Gunther says he has been waiting to get this off his chest for a very long time. Gunther tells Zayn that for his entire WWE career, when he was at his peak, Zayn screwed him when he was Intercontinental Champion at WrestleMania, when he was the special referee in his match against Cody, even when he was his partner at Madison Square Garden. Gunther says Zayn is the only reason why Zayn is not standing as WWE Champion.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Out comes Owens with Nick Aldis and Owens says he left, just like Gunther asked. Owens says he got Aldis, he told Aldis what Gunther did which is threaten him, his career. He was thinking it&#8217;s the Holiday season, he is very thankful that he got the chance to get in the ring after 17 months off and Gunther tells him he is the career killer. Owens says he asked if he would slap Gunther in the ring and that would start a fight but he knows Aldis wouldn&#8217;t like that. Owens says he spoke to Aldis and Aldis liked his idea. Aldis says he thought Owens against Gunther tonight is a good idea.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Owens says he is thankful that he gets to beat Gunther tonight and happy Thanksgiving. Kevin&#8217;s music hits and he leaves.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We cut to an interview from earlier today of Cathy Kelley and Jade Cargill. He says Kelly that she plans on being her, since she set foot in WWE, she has seen Flair. And deep down inside, Jade is everything that Flair wants to be.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from commercial, we see The Rock&#8217;s announcement on the Pat McAfee Show announcing that he will be at Survivor Series.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>WarGames Advantage Match &#8211; Jade Cargill vs. Charlotte Flair</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The bell rings and we are under way. Jade with right hands but Flair throws Jade into the turnbuckle. Jade with right hands but Flair throws her to the ropes and Flair with a clothesline.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Flair grabs Jade but Jade with right hands. Jade goes for a suplex but Flair lands on her feet. Flair with a kick to the side of the head and Flair with a kick to the face. Flair climbs the second rope but Jade trips her up. Jade with right hands and she goes for the cover but Flair kicks out.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from commercial, Flair with chops to the chest. Flair on the ring apron and she hits Jade with a boot to the face. Flair climbs the top rope and lands a cross body. She goes for the cover but Jade kicks out. Flair with an overhead throw. Flair goes for a big boot but Jade moves out of the way. Jade lifts Flair up and slams her onto the mat. She goes for the cover but Flair kicks out.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Jade goes for a kick but Flair moves out of the way and Flair with a spear. Flair climbs the top rope and lands a moon sault. She goes for the cover but Jade kicks out. Flair grabs Jade but Jade kicks her away. Jade with a pump kick. She goes for the cover but Flair kicks out. Jade goes for Jaded but Flair rolls through it and grabs Jade by the leg. Flair with the Figure Four but Jade makes it to the ropes. Jade removes the turnbuckle pad and Flair with a German suplex. Flair with the Natural Selection. She goes for the cover but Jade kicks out. Flair with right hands and Jade with right hands. Jade goes for a chokeslam but Flair lands on her feet and Flair with a big boot. Flair runs towards Jade but Jade trips her and Flair hits the exposed turnbuckle pad. Jade goes for the cover and gets the pin.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Winner: Jade Cargill</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We cut backstage and Kevin Owens is stopped by Candice LeRae. She tells him that she knows what he is trying to do is pathetic but Johnny is next. Owens says he will overlook the fact that she slapped him. He says he genuinely likes her but when she sees Zayn that he is going to take that title from him and for her lovely husband, to tell him to stay out of his way. And he needs to get a better haircut.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A War Raiders promo airs where they talk about Bakusai.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from commercial, Green says their friendship is done but she did get her Crown Jewel ring back. In comes Blake Monroe, she tells Green that Green went from rags to riches back to rags. Chelsea slaps Monroe and in comes Tiffany Stratton and she hits Green from behind. Stratton grabs the Crown Jewel ring and steals it from her. Blake hits Green and in come WWE officials who break it up.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Bakusai (Shinsuke Nakamura and Kyoki) vs. War Raiders (Erik and Ivar)</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The bell rings and we are under way. Kyoki and Erik start the match. In come Nakamura and Ivar but Bakusai double team him. Nakamura and Ivar are tagged in. Nakamura with a running knee and Ivar to the outside. Nakamura to the outside but Ivar throws him into the barricade.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from commercial, Nakamura and Erik are n the ring. Nakamura with a flying knee to the face. Kyoki and Ivar are tagged in. Kyoki with a cross body onto Ivar and a cross body onto Erik. Kyoki to the ropes and a drop kick onto Ivar. Kyokiwith a clothesline. He grabs Ivar by the beard and twists it. Kyoki with a drop kick and a DDT. Kyoki climbs the top rope and lands a drop kick. He goes for the cover but Erik breaks it up. Nakamura gets in the ring but Erik with a clothesline and both men to the outside of the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Out comes Haku and that distracts Kyoki. He turns around, Ivar with a spin kick. He goes for the cover and gets the pin.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Winners: War Raiders</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Out come the MFTs from behind and they attack the War Raiders.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We cut to the back, Nick Aldis is with Cody Rhodes. He tells Aldis that he will announce the member for team USA tonight. In comes Rey Fenix and he tells Cody he just saw CM Punk walk towards the ring. In come Miz and Kit Wilson. They cut a promo on Rey Fenix and Fenix says Kit Wilson is toxic. They argue and Nick Aldis makes a match tonight between Kit Wilson and Rey Fenix.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from commercial, Cathy Kelely is backstage with Sami Zayn, Johnny Gargano and Candice LeRae. Zayn says they are all vultures, gunning for his title. He says he hears everyone and sees everyone. He says no one deserves anything, except for Gargano. He says he respects LeRae for telling Owens to his face how it is. Zayn says he would not be WWE Champion if he just stayed away and that is not how they do things.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Out comes CM Punk to the ring. As he is about to speak, out comes Cody Rhodes. They begin to talk and Punk introduces the fifth member of for Team USA at WarGames. Out comes Haksaw Jim Duggan and Cody shakes his head.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cody and Punk argue and go back and forth about the decision of having Haksaw Jim Duggan in the team. Cody agrees and says that Duggan is the fifth member.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A video package of Team Mexico airs and Duggan asks them if they want him to be part of the team against Team Mexico at Survivor Series. Duggan says no and leaves the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">With Cody and Punk still in the ring, out comes Trick Williams and Lil Yachty to the ring. Lil Yachty makes a case for Trick Williams to be in Team USA at Survivor Series because he is the United States champion. Cody and Punk seem to agree and they all hug.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Trick Williams with Lil Yachty vs. Damian Priest</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The bell rings and we are under way. Priest with right hands and he goes for another right hand but Trick with a neck breaker. Trick clotheslines Priest over the top rope and to the outside of the ring. Priest with a right hand but Trick throws him onto the announce table. Trick goes for a big boot but Priest hits him with the ring bell. The referee sees it and calls for the bell.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Winner: By disqualification, Trick Williams</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Priest hits Trick after the match and out come WWE officials to break it up.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from commercial, Cody Rhodes is with CM Punk backstage. In comes Nick Aldis who tells them that Trick Williams is hurt. Cody and Punk are angry and we cut to the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Rey Fenix def. Kit Wilson with The Miz</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Kevin Owens def. Gunther</strong></p>
